# /etc/security/group.conf snippet — grant the seated user the
# `nostr-auth-greeter` supplementary group at session-open time so the
# gnome-shell running the lock screen (session-mode unlock-dialog) can
# read /run/nostr-auth/greeter/current.json + current.png + avatar.png
# while a NIP-46 re-auth is pending.
#
# Install as:
#   sudo install -m 0644 nostr-auth-greeter.group.conf.sample \
#     /etc/security/group.conf.d/50-nostr-auth-greeter.conf
# (or append its non-comment line to /etc/security/group.conf on
# distros that don't ship a /etc/security/group.conf.d drop-in dir).
#
# Precondition: /etc/pam.d/login (and the display-manager service, e.g.
# gdm-password / gdm-launch-environment) must `auth optional
# pam_group.so` — Debian/Ubuntu ships /etc/pam.d/login with pam_group
# already enabled; other distros may need to add the line by hand.
#
# Format: services;terminals;users;times;groups
# The wildcards below give any user, on any tty/service, at any time,
# the `nostr-auth-greeter` group at session start.  Tighten `users` to
# a specific member list (e.g. `n_bizarro|n_alice`) if only certain
# accounts should be able to render the QR panel on their lock screen.
#
# See docs/reviews/greeter-artifact-secret-confidentiality-2026-09-22.md
# (beads nostrc-3c7n, references nostrc-zcll.6).
*; *; *; Al0000-2400; nostr-auth-greeter
